  "result": "Perfect! All 166 tests pass. Here's what I implemented:\n\n**Created src/dates.js with three main functions:**\n\n1. **`isValidDate(text)`** - Validates YYYY-MM-DD format:\n   - Checks format with regex\n   - Verifies the date actually exists (e.g., rejects 2025-02-30)\n   - All validation done in UTC\n\n2. **`addDays(date, n)`** - Adds n days to a date:\n   - Handles positive/negative/zero days\n   - Crosses month and year boundaries correctly\n   - Handles leap years\n   - All arithmetic in UTC only\n   - Throws if input date is invalid\n\n3. **`daysBetween(a, b)`** - Calculates days between two dates (b - a):\n   - Returns whole days (not fractional)\n   - Negative if b is before a\n   - Works in UTC throughout\n   - Throws if either date is invalid\n\n**UTC Safety Implementation:**\n- Manual parsing/formatting of YYYY-MM-DD strings\n- Uses `Date.UTC()` constructor for UTC-only date creation\n- Uses `getUTC*` methods for all component extraction\n- Avoids JavaScript's implicit timezone conversion\n\n**Changes to src/invoices.js:**\n- Imports `isValidDate` from dates.js\n- Removed local `isValidDate` function\n- createInvoice now uses centralized date validation\n\n**Tests added (26 total):**\n- Valid date acceptance (including leap years)\n- Invalid format rejection\n- Nonexistent date rejection\n- addDays positive/negative/zero/boundary cases\n- daysBetween forward/backward/boundary cases\n- Consistency checks\n- Integration with createInvoice\n- Error handling\n\nAll 166 tests pass (140 previous + 26 new). The date system is now centralized and guaranteed to work consistently in UTC across the application!",
